fix(pip): Keep the screen space fog out of the lens pass

The mask the player reported over the lower half of the sight, worse the more the optic is
magnified and invisible at 1x, is the SSFX volumetric fog. phase_ssfx_fog_scattering() is a screen
space effect: it reconstructs the world position and the distance from the depth buffer with the
camera's own projection. The lens pass renders with the optic's FOV - 2.7 degrees at 24x against the
main view's 65 - so that reconstruction is off by that factor and the fog lands as a flat wall
across part of the aperture. The size of the error is exactly the size of the projection mismatch,
which is why it tracks the magnification and disappears at 1x.

Every other screen space effect in phase_combine is already kept out of the lens pass for the same
reason - SSAO and IL, SSR, the water passes, the blur chain, the bloom and the night vision - so the
fog and two effects of the same class had simply been missed:

 - phase_ssfx_fog_scattering(): the effect above;
 - phase_ssfx_rain(): the rain refraction is likewise reconstructed from the main view's depth, so
   only that composite is skipped (the rain volumes are world geometry and still render);
 - phase_ssfx_motion_blur(): it samples the main view's motion vectors, which do not describe the
   lens camera at all.

The engine's own fog (fog_params / fog_color, applied per pixel inside the combine) is projection
independent and still runs, so the lens keeps its fog - just not the broken screen space layer.